{"title":"Tysons Corner (Alaska) fact of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/968383190/0/marginalrevolution~Tysons-Corner-Alaska-fact-of-the-day.html","date":1787942257000,"content":"<blockquote><p>The centerpiece is Tysons Corner Center, today the eighth largest mall in the country, and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://wtop.com/business-finance/2020/07/dc-area-now-leads-for-suburban-office-space-led-by-tysons/\" target=\"_blank\">one of the largest</a> sub-city-sized markets for office space. It is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/economy/tysons-corner-center-just-a-piece-of-oil-backed-alaska-wealth-funds-portfolio/2011/09/21/gIQARE3wtK_story.html\" target=\"_blank\">half-owned</a> by the Alaska Permanent Fund, which is the state-owned corporation that invests oil revenue on behalf of Alaska’s citizens, and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://investing.macerich.com/news-releases/news-release-details/macerich-completes-710-million-refinancing-tysons-corner-center\" target=\"_blank\">half-owned</a> by Macerich, a giant REIT, which is in turn owned by hundreds of large institutional investors and many individuals.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>This <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.thenewatlantis.com/publications/you-probably-own-this-7-eleven\" target=\"_blank\">very interesting essay</a> by Joseph Lawler argues that liquid real estate markets, and distanced ownership, militate against beauty.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/tysons-corner-alaska-fact-of-the-day.html\">Tysons Corner (Alaska) fact of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img 